| `transports.serve.shutdown_grace_seconds` | number | `10` | a number, 0 or more and at most `threading.TIMEOUT_MAX` | `scripts/resource_limits.py` (`serve_limits`) for `api/rest_fastapi/serve.py` and `api/grpc/server.py` (`serve`) | Sets how long the REST or gRPC server lets the calls in flight finish after the first SIGTERM or SIGINT before it ends them. In the gRPC and MCP servers a second signal ends the session of every `run_bounded` child still running, then the process, by that signal; under uvicorn (REST) the second signal goes to uvicorn first, so a second SIGINT forces its exit while a second SIGTERM waits out the grace before it reaches that handler. The MCP server reads it but has no call to drain: it stops between requests. Absent, the server writes `[using default] transports.serve.shutdown_grace_seconds = 10` to stderr. | how long one call may take: the calling client's deadline | always |
